    "A": "Investigate a sparse-obstacle approach, but prioritize reducing overhead and validating it against the measured baseline: all four measured sparse inclusion-exclusion variants are slower (0.109–0.143 s) than the dense baseline (0.081 s). Profile likely causes and benchmark alternatives such as a compact flat bitmap plus row-wise DP, avoiding an N×N vector-of-vectors allocation where appropriate. Preserve correctness for arbitrary valid blocked coordinates, duplicates, and blocked endpoints; do not assume sparse is faster merely from asymptotic complexity.",
    "B": "Explore a distinct optimization: retain row-wise dynamic programming while exploiting sparse obstacles, e.g. process only affected rows/segments or use a flat representation, and compare against baseline and A/C proposals. The observed O(m²) obstacle inclusion-exclusion variants are slower than baseline on this run, so avoid adopting them without measured gains. Ensure every valid input, including duplicates and blocked start/destination, matches the reference.",
